# --- card title/taxonomy generation (regenerable Fireworks output) ---
# The DERIVED artifacts are tracked (card-taxonomy.json is curated and load-bearing; the
# titles are folded into rag/pipeline/cardsPool.app.json by assemble-card-titles.py). The raw
# per-batch shards are not — they are large, reproducible, and only exist to make the run
# resumable.
rag/pipeline/taxonomy-probe/
rag/pipeline/card-titles/
rag/bank/*.pre-rematch.bak

# DepEd card pipeline — large regenerable intermediates.
# NOTE: a `#` only starts a comment at the START of a line. These patterns used to carry
# trailing "# why" notes, which made each one a literal pattern containing spaces and a hash
# that matched nothing — so 184 MB of embedding caches and 24 MB of assembled pool showed up
# as untracked, one `git add .` away from the history. Keep every note on its own line.
# 20 MB of raw module text; comes from the harvest
rag/pipeline/deped-modules.jsonl
# 60 MB top-8 shortlists; rebuilt by match-illustrations.py
rag/pipeline/card-illustrations.json
rag/pipeline/card-illustrations.v1.json
rag/pipeline/card-illustrations.chosen.v1.json
# rebuilt locally, free
rag/pipeline/illustration-items.json
# embedding caches (merge-card-banks.py rebuilds them from a running llama-server)
rag/pipeline/*-vectors.npy
# assembled from deped-cards-v3/ (tracked) instantly — see also rag/.gitignore, whose
# `!*.json` would otherwise un-ignore this one
rag/pipeline/cardsPool.deped*.json
# (cardsPool.merged.json IS tracked — it is the input to wire-app-pool.py, and
#  rebuilding it needs a running llama-server plus ~8 min of embedding.)
# A/B generation samples
rag/pipeline/ab-*/
rag/pipeline/ab2-*/
rag/pipeline/ab3-*/
# superseded v1 generation
rag/pipeline/deped-cards/
# pre-polish backup
rag/pipeline/deped-cards-v3.prepolish/
# multi-GB batch outputs
rag/pipeline/imagegen/*.jsonl
!rag/pipeline/imagegen/worklist.jsonl
# 1024px PNGs; webp is what ships
rag/pipeline/imagegen/raw/
# incomplete until all 3 batches land
rag/pipeline/imagegen/webp/
card-cats/
